 "_title": "CCC GE credit for standardized examinations — AP, IB & CLEP",
 "_source": "ESLEI 24-35 (CCCCO Equitable Student Learning/ESS, 2024-06-25) Annual Updates — IB (App. B, title 5 §55052.5), CLEP (App. C, §55052.5), AP (App. D, §55052 / AB 1985). Foundational AP policy: AA 17-20 (2017-03-30) + FAQ AA 17-33 (2017-06-16); being codified via CCR Title 5 NPRM (45-day notice 2026-01-12). Source docs in docs/reference/.",
 "_ge_framework": "title 5 §55063 four divisions (2024 labels): Natural Sciences, Social/Behavioral Sciences, Arts and Humanities, Language and Rationality. N/A (Not Applicable) -> the college may award elective credit.",
 "_policy_notes": [
  "Minimum passing score per program (AP>=3; IB 4-5 by exam; CLEP 50-63 by exam); GE-Area credit awarded at the indicated minimum units (colleges may award more / additional / alternative).",
  "Course-to-course credit is a LOCAL faculty decision; the GE Area is the statewide constant. Where no GE Area matches, the college may award elective credit (origin of the MAP 'elective bucket').",
  "areas_all=true means credit is awarded in ALL listed areas together (e.g. AP English Literature = 6 units across Language and Rationality AND Arts and Humanities); otherwise any one listed area qualifies ('X or Y')."
 ],
